    "aliases": ["FaithJudge Hallucinations Benchmark", "FaithJudge Leaderboard"],
    "description": "Tests hallucination in retrieval-augmented generation on three tasks: summarization, question answering from passages, and data-to-text writing from JSON. Prompts come from FaithBench (72 summarization items) and RAGTruth (150 summarization, 139 question answering, 150 data-to-text). A model judge sees human-annotated hallucinations in other models' answers to the same item, then marks the target's answer. The headline is the overall hallucination rate.",
